> Interpretation and limits

Complete model shape, finite stochastic rows and every symbol are validated
through the shared native validator. Strict improvements retain the smallest
predecessor/final state at ties; this local rule is not a whole-path
lexicographic promise. Table and candidate budgets are explicit. The
illustrative symptom labels do not make this a medical model.

All programs are complete editable C++ sources; figures are local files. Actual
traces and selected counts come from the producing native kernels, not an
independent report reconstruction.

> References

- [Rabiner, A tutorial on hidden Markov models|https://doi.org/10.1109/5.18626]

